<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114095" body-key="">*<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλάδω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>exult loudly,</i> assumed as pres.
			of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέχλᾱδα,</span> wh. occurs thrice in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλίνικος . . κεχλαδώς,</span>
			of a triumphal hymn, <i><span class="en">
				<u>O.</u>
				9.2
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεχλάδοντας ἥβα,</span> of two
			young heroes, <i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				4.179
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέχλαδεν κρόταλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Dith.Oxy.</u>
					2.10
				</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεχληδέναι:
		ψοφεῖν.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
